From: termux-glibc-mesa <termux-glibc-mesa@local>
Subject: [PATCH] egl,glx: default to zink on Android/KGSL

On Adreno devices exposed through KGSL (Android's out-of-tree DRM
driver) there is no upstream freedreno *gallium* KMD: the only supported
render path is Turnip (Vulkan, tu_knl_kgsl.cc) reached through zink via
Kopper.  Upstream only falls back to zink *after* the in-tree driver has
already failed to initialize, which is a wasted round of screen setup
and, on GLX, frequently never happens at all because
loader_get_driver_for_fd() cannot resolve a driver name for a KGSL fd.

Make zink the preferred driver unless the user explicitly overrode it
via MESA_LOADER_DRIVER_OVERRIDE or GALLIUM_DRIVER.

  * EGL: disp->Options.Zink defaults to TRUE when
    MESA_LOADER_DRIVER_OVERRIDE is unset (or set to "zink"), instead of
    only when it is exactly "zink".
  * GLX: pre-elect GLX_DRIVER_ZINK_YES in the same situation, so Kopper
    is used from the first screen probe.

Without this, GL clients on Adreno+KGSL silently end up on llvmpipe or
fail to create a screen.
---
--- a/src/egl/main/eglapi.c
+++ b/src/egl/main/eglapi.c
@@ -684,7 +684,12 @@
                  "Found 'LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE' set, will use a CPU renderer");
 
       const char *env = os_get_option("MESA_LOADER_DRIVER_OVERRIDE");
-      disp->Options.Zink = env && !strcmp(env, "zink");
+      /* Prefer zink unless the user explicitly asked for something else.
+       * On Android/KGSL this is the only hardware path (Turnip via
+       * Kopper); upstream would only reach it after a failed probe.
+       */
+      disp->Options.Zink = (!env || !strcmp(env, "zink")) &&
+                           !os_get_option("GALLIUM_DRIVER");
 
       const char *gallium_hud_env = os_get_option("GALLIUM_HUD");
       disp->Options.GalliumHudWarn =
--- a/src/glx/glxext.c
+++ b/src/glx/glxext.c
@@ -989,7 +989,12 @@
    Bool kopper = !debug_get_bool_option("LIBGL_KOPPER_DISABLE", false);
 #endif
 
-   if (env && !strcmp(env, "zink"))
+   /* Prefer zink unless the user explicitly asked for something else.
+    * On Android/KGSL the in-tree freedreno gallium KMD is absent, and
+    * loader_get_driver_for_fd() cannot name a driver for a KGSL fd, so
+    * electing zink up-front is the only way Kopper gets used.
+    */
+   if (!env || !strcmp(env, "zink"))
       glx_driver |= GLX_DRIVER_ZINK_YES;
 
    dpyPriv->drawHash = __glxHashCreate();
